4933.text:
4933 cōráyati , cṓr° 'steals' Mn. [ cōrá -¹] Pa. cōrēti ; NiDoc. coridemi 'I stole', coridaǵa 'theft';
Pk. cōria - 'stolen'; Gy. eur. čor - 'to steal', WPah. bhal. ċornū , cam. cōrṇā , N. cornu , °rāunu , B. corā , °rāna , Mth. corab , °rāeb , H. cornā (whence intr. curnā 'to be stolen'),
G. corvũ , M. ċorṇẽ , Ko. cortā . Addenda: cōráyati: S.kcch. corṇū 'to steal', WPah.kṭg. (kc.) ċornõ ; kc. ċoriṇo 'to hide oneself, abscond', ċoria , °iε 'stealthily'; J. corwṇu 'to be concealed or stolen';
Garh. cornu 'to steal'.

10074.text:
10074 mā́rgati 'seeks, requests' MBh. [NiDoc. points to mā́rgati rather than mr̥gyáti 'seeks' lex.: S. L. WPah.
with a ← EP. — mārga -] Pa. maggati 'hunts for, seeks'; NiDoc. margaṁti 3 pl., margidavo ger. 'to seek'; Pk. maggaï 'asks for';
Gy. eur. mang - 'to ask for, beg', arm. mang - 'to ask
for', pal. mángăr 'wants, wishes, loves'; K. mangun 'to

ask for', S. maṅaṇu ; L. maṅgaṇ 'to request', mult.
(from pres. part.) maṅgendā m. 'betrothed man'; P. maṅgṇā 'to ask for', ludh. maṅganā ; WPah.bhal. maggṇū 'to beg'; Ku. māṅṇo 'to ask for, ask in marriage';
N. māgnu 'to ask for', A. māgiba , B. māgā , māṅgā , Or. māgibā , Mth. mā̃gab , Bhoj. mā̃gal , OAw. māṁgaï , lakh. mā̃gab ; H. māgnā , mā̃gnā 'to demand,
ask in marriage'; OMarw. māgaï 'asks for', G. māgvũ , mā̃gvũ , M. māgṇẽ , Ko. māgtā ; Si. mägum-a 'seeing,
vision' (semant. cf. vḗnati and Sk. vindáti ~ Bal. gindag 'to see'). mārgaṇa-¹, mārgaṇa-², *mārgayitr̥-, mārgya-;
*unmārgati . Addenda: mā́rgati [Pa. maggati etc. rather from mr̥gyáti (T. Burrow BSOAS xxxviii 59) which accounts also
for ă of S. L. P. WPah. verb: mārgati is sanskritization
from Pa. Pk. magg - on analogy of Pa. Pk. magga -: mārga -. NiDoc. margidavo ← Sk. mārg - (T. Burrow loc.cit. f.n. 1)] S.kcch. maṅgṇū 'to ask for', WPah.kṭg. (kc.) maṅgṇõ 'to ask for, beg', J. māṅgṇu , Wkc. mɔṅgṇo ,
caus. məgauṇõ 'to procure, send for'.
